===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|hord}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hord|t=an accumulation of valuable objects cached for preservation or future use; treasure; hoard}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*huzdą|t=treasure; hoard}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kusdʰo-}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|Hort|t=hoard; refuge}}, {{cog|is|hodd|t=treasure}}, {{cog|la|custos|t=guard; keeper}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hidden]] [[supply]] or [[fund]].
#: ''a '''hoard''' of provisions; a '''hoard''' of money''
# {{lb|en|archaeology}} A [[cache]] of [[valuable]] objects or [[artefact]]s; a [[trove]].

